From: postmarketOS mojito port
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: codecs: wcd937x: make the RX HPH Mode names match the values

The control writes the item number into hph_mode, an enum wcd_clsh_mode. The
name table had an extra "CLS_H_INVALID" entry and swapped the last two names, so
for example "CLS_AB" selected CLS_H_LOHIFI. List the names in enum order.
---
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd937x.c	2026-11-27 07:57:55.517255924 +0500
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd937x.c	2026-11-27 07:57:55.535149090 +0500
@@ -1369,8 +1369,8 @@
 }
 
 static const char * const rx_hph_mode_mux_text[] = {
-	"CLS_H_NORMAL", "CLS_H_INVALID", "CLS_H_HIFI", "CLS_H_LP", "CLS_AB",
-	"CLS_H_LOHIFI", "CLS_H_ULP", "CLS_AB_LP", "CLS_AB_HIFI",
+	"CLS_H_NORMAL", "CLS_H_HIFI", "CLS_H_LP", "CLS_AB", "CLS_H_LOHIFI",
+	"CLS_H_ULP", "CLS_AB_HIFI", "CLS_AB_LP",
 };
 
 static const struct soc_enum rx_hph_mode_mux_enum =
